"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[1050],{438:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"","params":[{"name":"settings","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"deps","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":79,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"enqueue","desc":"Writes a ticket and its lane index, rolling back on any failure so a partial\\nenqueue never leaves a user reserved against a ticket that does not exist.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"request","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":234,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_tryQuickPlay","desc":"Tries to backfill one ticket into a live match.\\n\\nThe order here is load-bearing, and it is the same shape as `_commit`:\\n\\n1. **Take the seat.** Atomic, so only one server can hold it.\\n2. **Take the ticket**, by the compare-and-set in `_release`. A lane worker\\n   may have claimed it into a fresh match a moment ago, in which case this\\n   fails and the player is already spoken for.\\n3. **Give the seat back** if step 2 lost, so a match we are not sending\\n   anybody to does not sit there holding capacity until the reservation\\n   lapses.\\n\\nDoing it the other way round, taking the ticket first, would take a player\\nout of the queue before knowing there was anywhere to put them.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"ticket","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"now","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":491,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_advanceQuickPlay","desc":"Runs the backfill search for every local ticket that is due one.\\n\\nTickets are collected before any of them is acted on, because a successful\\nbackfill removes its entry from `_localTickets` and mutating that while\\niterating it is undefined.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"now","desc":"","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"mono","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":554,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_shouldWiden","desc":"Whether this lane should read the bands either side of it as well as its own.\\n\\nBand boundaries are hard walls, which is the price of splitting by rating,\\nand two cases are worth paying to cross:\\n\\n- **Too thin to match.** A band holding a handful of players has nothing to\\n  gain from privacy and everything to gain from the pool next door. This is\\n  also what rescues a lone player at the top of the ladder, whose band can\\n  hold nobody else at all, long before a merge would.\\n- **Too stale.** Once the anchor\'s rating window has relaxed past the width\\n  of the band, the players it should now reach are by definition outside it.\\n\\nNeither is free, so neither is the default: a busy band that is still turning\\nplayers over reads only itself.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"owned","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"now","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":683,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_readCandidates","desc":"Reads the lane\'s candidates, oldest first.\\n\\nReturns the count from the lane\'s own map alongside them, which is what the\\nscaler judges this lane\'s depth by, and the count from everything this lane\\nis responsible for, which is what decides whether the lease is worth keeping.\\nCandidates borrowed from a neighbour count towards neither: they belong to a\\nlane somebody else is holding.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"owned","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"now","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ Candidate }"},{"desc":"","lua_type":"number"},{"desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":706,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_claimTicket","desc":"Moves one ticket from `Queued` to `Claimed`, repairing stale claims on the\\nway.\\n\\nA claim past its deadline means its owner stopped. What it left behind\\ndepends on how far it got: if the referenced match reached `Ready`, the\\nplayers are genuinely matched, so the ticket is finalized under that match\\nrather than stolen. If the match is still `Claiming` past its own deadline it\\nnever committed, so it is marked `Aborted` and the ticket is taken.\\n\\nTickets whose origin server has stopped heartbeating are refused, since a\\nmatch containing them could not be delivered.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"candidate","desc":"","lua_type":"Candidate"},{"name":"matchId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"owned","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any?\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":817,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_commit","desc":"Turns a group of candidates into a committed match, or into nothing.\\n\\nThe order of these steps is load-bearing:\\n\\n1. **Sort the ticket ids.** Two workers contending for overlapping tickets\\n   acquire them in the same order and so cannot deadlock.\\n2. **Write the `Claiming` record.** A crash after this leaves a record\\n   another worker can resolve, rather than claims pointing at nothing.\\n3. **Claim every ticket.** Any refusal aborts and returns the rest to\\n   `Queued`. No hook has run yet, so nothing needs compensating.\\n4. **Validate the lease** before doing anything expensive.\\n5. **Run `finalize`.** The only step that yields and the only one with side\\n   effects outside Muster. The lease is renewed first so a slow hook cannot\\n   outlive it, the return value is validated and size-checked, and the lease\\n   is validated **again** afterwards because time passed.\\n6. **Compare-and-set `Claiming` to `Ready`.** Guarded on server id, lease\\n   epoch and deadline together, so a worker that lost its lease cannot commit\\n   even if it reaches this line. This is the linearization point: before it\\n   the match does not exist, after it it does.\\n7. **Then** mark tickets matched, unlock parties, and announce.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"group","desc":"","lua_type":"{ Candidate }"},{"name":"owned","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":931,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_deliver","desc":"Delivers a committed match to this server, if it holds any of the players.\\n\\nDeduplicated on matchId, so a match arriving by commit, by announcement and\\nby poll fires the signal once.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"envelope","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"source","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"dedupe","desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":1140,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"step","desc":"One pass: upkeep on local tickets, lane acquisition, then a scan of each held\\nlane.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1271,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_advanceListings","desc":"Heartbeats whichever listings this server is hosting. Only reaches for the\\nservice if it has already been built, so a lobby server that never hosts\\nanything pays nothing.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"mono","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":1293,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"start","desc":"","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1306,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"stop","desc":"Stops the loop and releases every lease this server holds, so another server\\ncan take the lanes immediately rather than after the 15-second timeout.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1333,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_release","desc":"Moves a ticket out of `Queued` and tears down everything that referenced it:\\nits lane index entry, its members\' user reservations, this server\'s local\\ncopy, and its party lock.\\n\\nThe compare-and-set is the interesting part. `_claimTicket` also only\\nsucceeds on a `Queued` ticket, so this is the single point where cancelling,\\nbackfilling and matching arbitrate against each other. Whichever writes\\nfirst wins, and the others see a state they cannot act on.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"requesterUserId","desc":"","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"ticketId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"state","desc":"The terminal state to write: `Cancelled` or `QuickPlayed`.","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"matchId","desc":"","lua_type":"string?\\n"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The ticket, or `nil` when it could not be taken.","lua_type":"any"},{"desc":"The failure to hand back, when there is one.","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":1384,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"Engine","desc":"The coordination layer behind [Matchmaker].\\n\\nEvery server runs the same loop and acts as both producer and worker; there\\nis no dedicated matchmaker server.\\n\\n### The loop\\n\\n1. **Enqueue.** Reserve each member\'s userId by compare-and-set so a player\\n   cannot hold two tickets, write the ticket, then write a denormalized copy\\n   into the lane\'s sorted map, keyed by queue time.\\n2. **Acquire.** Take leases on the lanes this server\'s own tickets landed in.\\n   The lease holder does the matching for that lane.\\n3. **Scan.** Read the oldest candidates and run [Matcher] over them.\\n4. **Commit.** Two-phase and fenced; see `_commit`.\\n5. **Deliver.** Announce the match to the servers holding its players. Those\\n   servers also poll, so delivery does not depend on the announcement.\\n\\n### Recovery\\n\\nState is recovered by expiry rather than cleanup:\\n\\n| Failure | Recovery |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Worker dies holding a lease | The lease expires after 15 s and the next holder takes it at a higher epoch, which rejects any late write from the dead one |\\n| Worker dies mid-commit | Claims expire; the next worker adopts the match if it committed, and aborts it if it did not |\\n| Producer dies with tickets queued | Heartbeats stop and the tickets expire within `ticketExpiration` |","source":{"line":33,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}}')}}]);